// ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Single-page strategy: this ONE URL answers every search need for
// Dujiangyan Panda Base — tickets, volunteer program, transport,
// best time, comparisons, nearby attractions, closure status, FAQ.
// All legacy URLs 301-redirect to the relevant #section on this page.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: "Is Dujiangyan Panda Base currently open?",
    a: "No. Dujiangyan Panda Base (都江堰中华大熊猫苑) closed on <strong>April 23, 2026</strong> for facility upgrades and renovation. The reopening date has not been announced. While it is closed, see our <a href=\"#alternatives\" class=\"text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline\">recommended alternatives</a> below.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the difference between Dujiangyan Panda Base and Chengdu Panda Base?",
    a: "Dujiangyan is quieter, has fewer pandas (~20), and is the only base near Chengdu offering a hands-on volunteer program. Chengdu Research Base is much larger (~200 pandas), has a famous panda nursery, and is easier to reach by subway. See the <a href=\"#comparison\" class=\"text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline\">full side-by-side comparison</a>.",
  },
  {
    q: "How much does the volunteer program cost?",
    a: "The volunteer program costs approximately CNY 700-900 per person and includes the entrance fee, uniform, gloves, lunch, and a certificate. See the <a href=\"#volunteer\" class=\"text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline\">volunteer section</a> for the full breakdown and booking tips.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I get to Dujiangyan Panda Base from Chengdu?",
    a: "The fastest way is the high-speed train from Xipu Station to Dujiangyan Station (20-30 min), then a 15-minute taxi to the base — about 1-1.5 hours total. Bus, taxi/ride-hailing, and organized tours are also options. See <a href=\"#getting-there\" class=\"text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline\">all four transport options</a> with costs.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I hold a baby panda?",
    a: "Direct holding is no longer permitted under current conservation guidelines. The volunteer program does allow you to sit next to a panda for a photo and get very close during feeding and enclosure care.",
  },
  {
    q: "When is the best time to visit?",
    a: "Spring (March-May) and autumn (September-November) offer the best weather and most active pandas. During summer, arrive early morning before the heat. Winter has the fewest crowds. See the <a href=\"#best-time\" class=\"text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline\">month-by-month guide</a>.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need to book tickets in advance?",
    a: "General admission can be bought at the gate, but booking online is recommended during peak seasons (summer and Chinese holidays). The volunteer program must be booked at least 1-2 weeks ahead. See <a href=\"#tickets\" class=\"text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline\">ticket details</a>.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is the base suitable for children?",
    a: "Yes, the base is family-friendly and the paths are stroller-friendly. The volunteer program has a minimum age of 12, but general visitors of all ages are welcome.",
  },
  {
    q: "What are the opening hours?",
    a: "Under normal operations the base is open daily from 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM, year-round. Arrive at opening time — pandas are most active in the morning.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the minimum age for volunteers?",
    a: "The volunteer program is open to ages 12-65. Participants under 18 must be accompanied by a parent or guardian.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need to speak Chinese to volunteer?",
    a: "Basic English is usually sufficient — most programs have English-speaking coordinators. Learning a few Chinese phrases can enhance the experience.",
  },
  {
    q: "What should I wear for the volunteer program?",
    a: "Comfortable clothes you don't mind getting dirty, closed-toe shoes, sunscreen, and insect repellent. The base provides a uniform or apron for volunteer activities.",
  },
  {
    q: "How far in advance should I book the volunteer program?",
    a: "At least 1-2 weeks in advance. During peak seasons (summer, Chinese holidays), spots can fill up 3-4 weeks ahead — Golden Week can fill a month in advance.",
  },
];

