                  <div class="bg-warm-50 rounded-xl p-3.5"><span class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-warm-500 block mb-1">Volunteer</span><span class={`font-semibold ${alt.volunteer ? "text-accent-700" : "text-warm-900"}`}>{alt.volunteer ? "Available" : "Not offered"}</span></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-3xl bg-warm-900 border border-warm-800 p-7 md:p-8">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">Booking tips while Dujiangyan is closed</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-warm-300 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong class="text-white">Panda Valley:</strong> book online in advance — there is no reliable on-site ticket window. Use the official English page at <a href="https://panda.org.cn/en/pandavalley/tickets" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-300 hover:text-white underline">panda.org.cn/en/pandavalley/tickets</a> or the WeChat mini-program 熊猫谷 (has an English toggle). Foreign visitors book with a passport number.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Wolong & Bifengxia:</strong> volunteer keeper programs are booked through authorized agencies or the CCRCGP's official channels — plan 1-2 weeks ahead in peak season.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">General:</strong> weekday mornings are always quieter; don't rely on walk-up tickets on weekends or Chinese holidays.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ DAILY RHYTHM ============ -->
  <section id="visit-guide" class="scroll-mt-28 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-28 reveal">
    <SectionHeader
      eyebrow="During Your Visit"
      title="A panda's day — plan around it"
      subtitle="Pandas follow a predictable rhythm. Time your visit right and you'll see them at their best."
    />
    <div class="mt-10 relative">
      <div class="absolute left-4 md:left-1/2 top-0 bottom-0 w-0.5 bg-warm-200 -translate-x-1/2 hidden md:block" />
      <div class="space-y-8">
        {rhythm.map((item) => (
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4 md:gap-8">
            <div class={`hidden md:flex w-1/2 justify-end ${item.active ? '' : 'md:order-2'}`}>
              {item.active && (
                <div class="text-right pr-8">
                  <Icon name={`fa6-solid:${item.icon}`} class="w-6 h-6 text-accent-600" />
                  <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-accent-800">{item.title}</h3>
                  <p class="text-sm text-warm-600 mt-1 max-w-xs ml-auto">{item.desc}</p>
                </div>
              )}
            </div>
            <div class={`shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold z-10 ${item.active ? 'bg-accent-500 text-white ring-4 ring-accent-100' : 'bg-warm-200 text-warm-600'}`}>
              {item.time.split(':')[0]}
            </div>
            <div class={`md:w-1/2 ${item.active ? '' : 'md:order-1 md:text-right md:pr-8'}`}>
              <div class="md:hidden mb-1"><Icon name={`fa6-solid:${item.icon}`} class="w-5 h-5 text-accent-600" /></div>
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-warm-500">{item.time}</p>
              <h3 class={`text-sm font-semibold mt-0.5 ${item.active ? 'text-accent-800' : 'text-warm-700'}`}>{item.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-warm-600 mt-1 leading-relaxed md:max-w-xs">{item.desc}</p>
              {!item.active && <div class="hidden md:block mt-1"><Icon name={`fa6-solid:${item.icon}`} class="w-5 h-5 text-warm-400" /></div>}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-20 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-warm-950">The base, zone by zone</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-warm-600">The park holds 40+ pandas (20+ on view) across four main zones, each a 5-10 minute walk apart, plus a shuttle. To dodge the tour groups, start at the entrance and work inward: Panpan Garden → Linze Garden → Diequan Garden → Shuangnan Garden.</p>
    <div class="mt-8 grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-warm-200 bg-warm-200">
      {zones.map((z) => (
        <div class="p-7 bg-white">
          <span class="text-[10px] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-accent-100 text-accent-800 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide">{z.highlight}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-warm-950">{z.name} <span class="text-warm-400 font-sans font-normal text-xs">({z.chinese})</span></h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">{z.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-3xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/60 p-7 md:p-8">
      <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-amber-900 mb-3">Before you go — things to know</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-warm-700 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>The base is <strong>hilly with many steps</strong> and not very wheelchair-friendly — if that's a concern, Panda Valley is the flatter alternative.</li>
        <li>Stone viewing fences are quite high: hold young children (under about 1.2 m) so they can see the pandas.</li>
        <li>Shuttle buses run within the park between the zones.</li>
        <li>Meals: the base canteen, nearby farmhouses, or in Dujiangyan city center. No need to stay overnight unless you're also visiting the Irrigation System or Mt. Qingcheng.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ PACKING CHECKLIST ============ -->
  <section class="bg-warm-100/40 py-20 md:py-28 reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Before You Go"
        title="Pack this, not that"
        subtitle="Six essentials that make the difference between a good visit and a great one."
      />
      <div class="mt-12 grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-warm-200 bg-warm-200">
        {packing.map((item) => (
          <div class={`p-7 ${item.must ? "bg-accent-50/60" : "bg-white"}`}>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <Icon name={`fa6-solid:${item.icon}`} class="w-6 h-6 text-accent-700 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-warm-950">{item.title}</h3>
                  {item.must && <span class="text-[10px] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-accent-600 text-white font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide">Must</span>}
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs text-warm-600 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">{item.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FIRST-HAND STORY + BOOKING ============ -->
  <section id="stories" class="scroll-mt-28 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-28 reveal">
    <SectionHeader
      eyebrow="Volunteer Stories"
      title="A panda keeper's day, first-hand"
      subtitle="Honest accounts from volunteers who cleaned enclosures, prepared bamboo, and hand-fed pandas at Dujiangyan."
    />
    <div class="mt-12 rounded-3xl border border-warm-200 bg-warm-100/40 p-8 md:p-12">
      <svg width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" class="text-accent-500/30 mb-6" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14.017 21v-7.391c0-5.704 3.731-9.57 8.983-10.609l.995 2.151c-2.432.917-3.995 3.638-3.995 5.849h4v10h-9.983zm-14.017 0v-7.391c0-5.704 3.748-9.57 9-10.609l.996 2.151c-2.433.917-3.996 3.638-3.996 5.849h3.983v10h-9.983z"/></svg>
      <p class="font-display text-lg md:text-xl text-warm-800 leading-relaxed">
        "When I signed up, I knew it would involve physical work — but the realness of it was the best part. By 8:30 AM we'd changed into the blue volunteer uniforms and gotten our safety briefing from an English-speaking coordinator. Cleaning enclosures is hard work (pandas eat up to 40 kg of bamboo a day, and what goes in must come out), but that's what makes it feel authentic. Then came the highlight around 11 AM: hand-feeding. A giant panda sitting two feet away, reaching out to take an apple from your hand, is surreal. The fee was CNY 800, including uniform, lunch, and a certificate."
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm font-semibold text-warm-900">— Sarah, volunteer, June 2026</p>
      <p class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-warm-200 text-sm text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Booking reality check:</strong> the base has no dedicated English booking site — the reliable paths are authorized travel agencies, your Chengdu hotel/hostel concierge, or the base's WeChat channel for Chinese speakers. Book 1-2 weeks ahead (3-4 weeks in peak season). Be wary of anyone quoting far above CNY 900 or guaranteeing you can "hold a baby panda" — that's no longer permitted.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
  <section id="faq" class="scroll-mt-28 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-28 reveal">
    <SectionHeader
      eyebrow="FAQ"
      title="Frequently asked questions"
      subtitle="Every common question about visiting, volunteering, and getting to Dujiangyan Panda Base."
    />
    <div class="mt-10">
      <Faq items={faqItems} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FULL-BLEED CTA ============ -->
